@FOR
.
=FOR
.
.FOR v = a TO b [STEP k] ... NEXT [v]. The variable is a BYTE or a WORD, and
.STEP is a constant, 1 when it is left out. STEP -1 counts down.
.
:FOR I = 0 TO 255
:  POKE $0400 + I, I
:NEXT
:FOR W% = 1000 TO 0 STEP -100
:  PRINT W%
:NEXT W%
.
.  - The body runs zero times when the range is empty.
.  - The test is made before the step, so FOR I = 0 TO 255 ends, and I never
.    wraps.
.  - After the loop, v holds the last value the body saw: 255 above.
.  - The TO value is read once, at the start.
